WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:18.277
Grace gazed at the big painting of a dancer.

2
00:00:18.278 --> 00:00:22.467
"That's beautiful!" she said.

3
00:00:22.468 --> 00:00:28.613
"When I get older, I want to be an artist."

4
00:00:28.614 --> 00:00:32.758
Grace and Dad were at an art museum in Boston.

5
00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:37.229
Grace suddenly noticed an empty frame on a wall.

6
00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:42.050
Then she noticed another empty frame.

7
00:00:42.051 --> 00:00:48.619
"Dad?" Grace asked. "Why are those frames empty?"

8
00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:52.050
"Their paintings are missing," said Dad.

9
00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.755
"Actually someone stole them."

10
00:00:54.756 --> 00:01:00.318
She gasped. "Really?"

11
00:01:00.319 --> 00:01:04.203
A museum guard walked over.

12
00:01:04.204 --> 00:01:09.284
"It was the biggest art theft in American history," he said.

13
00:01:09.285 --> 00:01:14.450
"When did it happen?" Grace asked.

14
00:01:14.451 --> 00:01:18.368
"March 18, 1990," said the guard.

15
00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:20.935
"Two thieves came late at night.

16
00:01:20.936 --> 00:01:25.210
They were dressed as police officers.

17
00:01:25.211 --> 00:01:31.769
So a museum guard let the men inside.

18
00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:43.496
The thieves stole paintings, sketches, a bronze eagle, and a small vase.

19
00:01:43.497 --> 00:01:48.725
All together the items are worth about fifty million dollars."

20
00:01:48.726 --> 00:01:54.234
"Whoa," said Grace. "That's a lot of money.

21
00:01:54.235 --> 00:01:59.648
I guess the thieves knew what to steal!"

22
00:01:59.649 --> 00:02:04.698
"The men did steal some valuable artwork," said the guard.

23
00:02:04.699 --> 00:02:10.026
"But they left more valuable artwork behind.

24
00:02:10.027 --> 00:02:14.499
Many people think the thieves didn't know much about art."

25
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:19.049
"Were the men ever caught?" asked Grace's dad.

26
00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.093
The guard shook his head.

27
00:02:21.094 --> 00:02:23.254
"The police had several suspects.

28
00:02:23.255 --> 00:02:26.441
But they never caught anyone.

29
00:02:26.442 --> 00:02:32.393
Workers at the museum decided to hang four empty frames.

30
00:02:32.394 --> 00:02:36.697
The frames remind everyone of the stolen paintings.

31
00:02:36.698 --> 00:02:40.852
We hope to get them back someday."

32
00:02:40.853 --> 00:02:43.863
Grace looked at Dad.

33
00:02:43.864 --> 00:02:48.027
"I don't want to be an artist anymore.

34
00:02:48.028 --> 00:02:59.064
I want to be a detective. And I want to solve this case!"

